        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Sec. 28.2\nComponents",
            "block_bbox": [
                107,
                777,
                226,
                824
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The various members of the Vertical Milling Machine of interest to the scraping operator are enumerated and described as follows:",
            "block_bbox": [
                106,
                845,
                496,
                936
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. The Column: The massive casting supporting the combined weight of the other machine members, in addition to the work piece, is known as the column, or frame. This member has two groups of bearing surfaces, viz: the lower group, or column ways, that guide the knee; the upper group, or head support ways, that guide the sliding head.",
            "block_bbox": [
                107,
                956,
                504,
                1181
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>2. The Sliding Head: This member is guided vertically by the ways of the head support located at the top of the column. The sliding head encloses the spindle.</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                105,
                1181,
                504,
                1293
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. The Knee: The component, guided by the ways of the column and vertically adjustable, is called the knee. It supports the saddle and table assembly.",
            "block_bbox": [
                106,
                1294,
                491,
                1340
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                551,
                778,
                915,
                822
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "4. The Plain Saddle: The lower bearing surfaces of this member are guided in cross-movement by the ways of the knee. The upper bearing surfaces guide the table in longitudinal movement.",
            "block_bbox": [
                524,
                822,
                920,
                955
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "5. The Table: The top surface of this member is provided with T-slots. This feature permits the work piece and also various attachments, such as the vise, the dividing head etc., to be secured by means of bolts.",
            "block_bbox": [
                524,
                956,
                933,
                1094
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The several members of the Sliding Head Vertical Milling Machine will be discussed in the order enumerated above. This is also the logical sequence of scraping operations.",
            "block_bbox": [
                523,
                1114,
                932,
                1228
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 10
        },
        {
